---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - Stephen Zweibel"
  description="Stephen Zweibel is an Associate Professor and Digital Scholarship Librarian at the CUNY Graduate Center and co-director of the CUNY AI Lab."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <div class="about-intro">
      <img
        src="/images/SteveProfile.jpeg"
        alt="Stephen Zweibel"
        width="192"
        height="192"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="lead">
          I'm an Associate Professor and Digital Scholarship Librarian at the Mina Rees Library of the CUNY Graduate Center. I help students and faculty plan and build digital projects, work with data, and make decisions about AI in research and teaching.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also co-direct the <a href="https://ailab.gc.cuny.edu/">CUNY AI Lab</a>. I built the CAIL Gateway, which connects the lab’s tools to a curated set of models. The lab also operates the zero-retention <a href="https://chat.ailab.gc.cuny.edu/">CAIL Sandbox</a>, a public <a href="https://ailab.gc.cuny.edu/models/">model registry</a>, and tools for classroom and research work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Current work</h2>

      <div class="work-item">
        <h3>CUNY AI Lab</h3>
        <p>
          I built the CAIL Gateway, which maintains the lab’s model catalog, routes requests across providers, tracks who is using what, and reports the budget they have left. My other work includes the <a href="https://tools.ailab.gc.cuny.edu/">Tools Portal</a>, agentic studios, model and provider policy, workshops, and public documentation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="work-item">
        <h3>Libraries and digital scholarship</h3>
        <p>
          At the library, I consult on digital projects, data analysis, visualization, web publishing, preservation, and research workflows. I serve as liaison to programs including Data Science, Digital Humanities, Demography, Computational Linguistics, and Geography/GIS.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="work-item">
        <h3>Research and writing</h3>
        <p>
          I write about how academic libraries and universities adopt AI while preserving professional judgment, privacy, and their public mission. I also work on agentic programming, computational literacy, and the practical governance of shared AI infrastructure. My 2026 article, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1353/pla.2026.a994555"><em>Do Artifacts Still Have Politics?</em></a>, develops that argument for academic libraries.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Selected projects</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <strong><a href="https://ailab.gc.cuny.edu/models/">CAIL Gateway</a></strong><br />
          The service I built behind CAIL’s tools, connecting them to the models we provide and keeping track of access and use.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><a href="https://ailab.gc.cuny.edu/">CUNY AI Lab</a></strong><br />
          Shared AI infrastructure, tools, documentation, and professional development for CUNY.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>DHRIFT</strong><br />
          Co-director of Digital Humanities Resource Infrastructure for Teaching Technology, supported by a 2023 NEH Level III Advancement Grant.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>DH Box</strong><br />
          Creator and developer of a cloud-based digital humanities platform supported by a 2015 NEH Start-Up Grant.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Open-source library and research tools</strong><br />
          Projects include Reference Agent, Augur, and workshop materials for programming and research APIs.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/projects">View all projects</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Teaching</h2>
      <p>
        I teach graduate courses in AI-assisted programming, Python for research, and JavaScript at the Graduate Center. The courses are project-oriented and designed for humanities and social science researchers. I also lead workshops on APIs, command-line tools, databases, text analysis, data management, and related research methods.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/teaching">Read more about my teaching</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Service</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Chair and primary author, CUNY Libraries Research Artificial Intelligence Task Force, 2024-25</li>
        <li>Author of <em>Evaluating AI Tools in Research Systems</em>, approved by the CUNY Office of Library Services in October 2025</li>
        <li>Member, CUNY Graduate Center IT Committee</li>
        <li>Chair, Mina Rees Library Web Services Steering Committee</li>
        <li>Reviewer for NEH Digital Humanities grants and academic journals</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>MS in Library and Information Science, Long Island University, 2010</li>
        <li>MA in Liberal Studies, Digital Humanities track, CUNY Graduate Center, 2016</li>
        <li>Bachelor of Liberal Arts, St. John's College, 2008</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="contact-card">
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:szweibel@gc.cuny.edu">szweibel@gc.cuny.edu</a><br />
          Mina Rees Library, Room 2313<br />
          The Graduate Center, CUNY<br />
          365 Fifth Avenue, New York, NY 10016
        </p>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/szweibel">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://libguides.gc.cuny.edu/prf.php?account_id=67188">LibGuides profile</a>
          <a href="https://www.gc.cuny.edu/people/stephen-zweibel">CUNY faculty page</a>
          <a href="/publications">Publications</a>
          <a href="/cv">Full CV</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .about-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .about-intro img {
    width: 12rem;
    height: 12rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .work-item {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .work-item h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .work-item p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .project-list li {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .project-list li:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .contact-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about-intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .about-intro img {
      width: 9rem;
      height: 9rem;
    }
  }
</style>
